access-log-summary:1.text:
{
  "analysis": "The log directory holds access.log (today), access.log.1 (yesterday) and error.log, which isn't needed. Lines are in combined log format: $1 is the client IP, $7 the request target (which may carry a query string, e.g. /api/orders?page=2) and $9 the status. Health checks look like `GET /healthz` from 10.0.0.1.",
  "plan": "Profile both files: line counts, number of /healthz lines, status code distribution, and the distinct request targets.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /var/log/webapp\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "wc -l access.log access.log.1\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -c ' /healthz' access.log access.log.1\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat access.log access.log.1 | awk '{print $9}' | sort | uniq -c\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat access.log access.log.1 | awk '{print $7}' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The logs are combined format. Before computing anything I want to make sure every line parses the same way (status in field 9, target in field 7) and that there are no malformed entries.",
  "plan": "Look for lines whose 9th field is not a 3-digit status, list the HTTP methods in use, and count lines per file.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /var/log/webapp\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk '$9 !~ /^[0-9][0-9][0-9]$/' access.log access.log.1 | head\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk '{print $6}' access.log access.log.1 | sort | uniq -c\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "wc -l access.log access.log.1\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "Format is standard combined log format; /healthz requests come from the load balancer (10.0.0.1, ELB-HealthChecker). Query strings appear in some targets (?page=2).",
  "plan": "Create /app/reports and write a filtered copy of both logs without /healthz requests into /tmp, then check its size and a sample.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p /app/reports\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /var/log/webapp/access.log /var/log/webapp/access.log.1 | grep -vE '\"[A-Z]+ /healthz[ ?]' > /tmp/clean.log\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "wc -l /var/log/webapp/access.log /var/log/webapp/access.log.1 /tmp/clean.log\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -n 3 /tmp/clean.log\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "I've seen the first lines of access.log. I should also check the older file and see how the health checks look across both files, and whether python3 is available as an option.",
  "plan": "Show the start of access.log.1 and the end of access.log, summarize health-check lines by IP/method/target, and check for python3.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -n 3 /var/log/webapp/access.log.1\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "tail -n 3 /var/log/webapp/access.log\n",
      "duration": 0.1
