access-log-summary:2.text:
{
  "analysis": "There are 323 lines total (183 + 140), 35 of them /healthz, so 288 real requests are expected. Field 9 is always a valid status (200-504). Targets include query strings like /search?q=boots and /api/export?fmt=csv, which must be stripped for the error report.",
  "plan": "Use the C locale for byte-wise sorting, save the non-healthz lines to a temp file, confirm the count, and look at per-IP counts.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "export LC_ALL=C\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat access.log access.log.1 | awk '$7 !~ /^\\/healthz/' > /tmp/filtered.log\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "wc -l /tmp/filtered.log\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk '{print $1}' /tmp/filtered.log | sort | uniq -c | sort -k1,1nr -k2,2\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The data looks clean: every status is a 3-digit code and the only health-check target is /healthz (35 lines). Expected total after exclusion is 323 - 35 = 288.",
  "plan": "Compute the summary numbers in a single awk pass over both files (skipping /healthz) and print them to the screen first so I can check them before writing the file.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk '$7 !~ /^\\/healthz(\\?|$)/ { n++; ip[$1]++; s[substr($9,1,1)]++ } END { print \"total\", n; print \"ips\", length(ip); for (k in s) print k \"xx\", s[k] }' access.log access.log.1\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk '$7 !~ /^\\/healthz(\\?|$)/ {print $1}' access.log access.log.1 | LC_ALL=C sort | uniq -c | LC_ALL=C sort -k1,1nr -k2,2\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "35 /healthz lines out of 323. All health checks appear as the bare path /healthz. I want to double-check there are no other variants (HEAD requests, other IPs) and see the full list of client IPs.",
  "plan": "Summarize the health-check lines by IP, method and status, and list all distinct client IPs with counts excluding /healthz.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -h '/healthz' access.log access.log.1 | awk '{print $1, $6, $7, $9}' | sort | uniq -c\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk '$7 != \"/healthz\" {print $1}' access.log access.log.1 | LC_ALL=C sort | uniq -c | LC_ALL=C sort -k1,1nr -k2,2\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The profile is clear: 323 lines, 35 /healthz, statuses from 200 to 504, and query strings on several targets. I can start producing the filtered data set.",
  "plan": "Create /app/reports, write the filtered lines to /tmp/clean.log, and print the status-class counts and top IPs (byte-wise tie-break via LC_ALL=C).",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p /app/reports\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat access.log.1 access.log | awk '$7 !~ /^\\/healthz(\\?|$)/' > /tmp/clean.log && wc -l /tmp/clean.log\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk '{print substr($9,1,1) \"xx\"}' /tmp/clean.log | sort | uniq -c\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk '{print $1}' /tmp/clean.log | LC_ALL=C sort | uniq -c | LC_ALL=C sort -k1,1nr -k2,2 | head -n 5\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

access-log-summary:3.text:
{
  "analysis": "The filtered file has 288 requests from 8 IPs. Top counts: 10.0.0.5 (66), then 10.0.0.12 and 10.0.0.7 tied at 57; byte-wise 10.0.0.12 < 10.0.0.7, so that is the order.",
  "plan": "Write traffic_summary.txt with a grouped command: total from wc, unique IPs via sort -u, per-class status counts, then top_ips in `<ip> <count>` form. Then display it.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p /app/reports\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "F=/tmp/requests.log; { echo \"total_requests=$(wc -l < $F)\"; echo \"unique_ips=$(awk '{print $1}' $F | sort -u | wc -l)\"; for k in 2 3 4 5; do echo \"status_${k}xx=$(awk -v k=$k 'substr($9,1,1)==k' $F | wc -l)\"; done; echo 'top_ips:'; awk '{print $1}' $F | sort | uniq -c | sort -k1,1nr -k2,2 | head -n 3 | awk '{print $2, $1}'; } > /app/reports/traffic_summary.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /app/reports/traffic_summary.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "288 requests, 8 distinct IPs. The top three with byte-wise tie-break are 10.0.0.5 66, 10.0.0.12 57, 10.0.0.7 57. LC_ALL=C is exported in this shell.",
  "plan": "Generate the counts with one awk END block into the summary file, append the top_ips header and the three IP lines, then print the result.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p /app/reports\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk '{t++; seen[$1]=1; cls=substr($9,1,1); cnt[cls]++} END {print \"total_requests=\" t; u=0; for (i in seen) u++; print \"unique_ips=\" u; print \"status_2xx=\" cnt[2]+0; print \"status_3xx=\" cnt[3]+0; print \"status_4xx=\" cnt[4]+0; print \"status_5xx=\" cnt[5]+0}' /tmp/requests.log > /app/reports/traffic_summary.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo 'top_ips:' >> /app/reports/traffic_summary.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cut -d' ' -f1 /tmp/requests.log | sort | uniq -c | sort -k1,1nr -k2,2 | head -3 | awk '{printf \"%s %s\\n\", $2, $1}' >> /app/reports/traffic_summary.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /app/reports/traffic_summary.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The filtered set is 288 lines (323 - 35), matching expectations. Per-IP counts show 10.0.0.5 first, then the 57-way tie between 10.0.0.12 and 10.0.0.7, which the C-locale sort already orders correctly.",
  "plan": "Compute the status class counts first so I can see them, then assemble the summary file with printf.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk '{print substr($9,1,1)}' /tmp/requests.log | sort | uniq -c\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p /app/reports && cd /app/reports\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "printf 'total_requests=%s\\nunique_ips=%s\\n' \"$(wc -l < /tmp/requests.log)\" \"$(cut -d' ' -f1 /tmp/requests.log | sort -u | wc -l)\" > traffic_summary.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "for k in 2 3 4 5; do printf 'status_%sxx=%s\\n' $k \"$(awk -v k=$k 'substr($9,1,1)==k' /tmp/requests.log | wc -l)\"; done >> traffic_summary.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "{ echo 'top_ips:'; cut -d' ' -f1 /tmp/requests.log | sort | uniq -c | sort -k1,1nr -k2,2 | head -n 3 | awk '{print $2\" \"$1}'; } >> traffic_summary.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat traffic_summary.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "Filtered data: 288 requests, 8 IPs, top three are 10.0.0.5 (66), 10.0.0.12 (57), 10.0.0.7 (57). I have everything needed for both reports.",
  "plan": "Write both reports in this step: the summary via awk plus the sorted IP list, and the 5xx-per-path CSV with query strings removed. Then print both.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p /app/reports && cd /app/reports\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk '{n++; ip[$1]++; s[substr($9,1,1)]++} END {printf \"total_requests=%d\\nunique_ips=%d\\n\", n, length(ip); for (k=2;k<=5;k++) printf \"status_%dxx=%d\\n\", k, s[k]; print \"top_ips:\"}' /tmp/requests.log > traffic_summary.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk '{print $1}' /tmp/requests.log | sort | uniq -c | sort -k1,1nr -k2,2 | head -n 3 | awk '{print $2, $1}' >> traffic_summary.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk '$9 ~ /^5/ {p=$7; sub(/\\?.*/, \"\", p); print p}' /tmp/requests.log | sort | uniq -c | sort -k1,1nr -k2,2 | awk 'BEGIN{print \"path,count\"} {print $2 \",\" $1}' > errors_by_path.csv\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat traffic_summary.txt errors_by_path.csv\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

