backup-cron-repair:2.text:
{"analysis": "Working on fixing the backup script.", "plan": "Create corrected backup script.", "commands": [{"keystrokes": "cat > /app/ops/backup.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash
EOF
", "duration": 0.1}], "task_complete": false}

{
  "analysis": "Issues visible: the script defaults CONF to /etc/app/backup.conf instead of /app/ops/backup.conf; backup.conf has `DEST_DIR = /var/backups/app` (spaces make bash run DEST_DIR as a command); the manifest is truncated as MANIFEST.txt but checksums are appended to MANIFEST; and the cron line has only four time fields before `root`.",
  "plan": "Confirm how the script fails as-is: check that the default config path doesn't exist, then run the script and capture the exit code.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -l /app/ops/backup.sh /etc/app/backup.conf 2>&1\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "/app/ops/backup.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "Four bugs: (1) default CONF path /etc/app/backup.conf is wrong; (2) `DEST_DIR = ...` in backup.conf is invalid shell assignment; (3) sha256sum appends to $DEST_DIR/MANIFEST rather than MANIFEST.txt; (4) the cron entry `30 2 * * root` lacks the day-of-week field.",
  "plan": "Fix all four with sed, install the cron snippet, then run the script without any environment override.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /app/ops\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -i 's/^DEST_DIR *= */DEST_DIR=/' backup.conf\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -i 's|/etc/app/backup.conf|/app/ops/backup.conf|' backup.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -i 's|>> \"$DEST_DIR/MANIFEST\"|>> \"$DEST_DIR/MANIFEST.txt\"|' backup.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -i 's/^30 2 \\* \\* root/30 2 * * * root/' backup.cron\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat backup.conf backup.cron; grep -n 'CONF=\\|MANIFEST' backup.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "./backup.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the main bugs (wrong default config path, spaces around = in DEST_DIR, MANIFEST vs MANIFEST.txt, missing cron field). Before editing, I want to rule out hidden characters such as CRLF line endings in the config and cron file, which would also break sourcing and cron.",
  "plan": "Show the config and cron snippet with cat -A and check permissions in /app/ops.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat -A /app/ops/backup.conf /app/ops/backup.cron\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /app/ops\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The script is short and has several bugs: wrong default config path, the DEST_DIR line in the config has spaces around '=', the checksum loop writes to MANIFEST instead of MANIFEST.txt, and the unquoted `for f in $(find ...)` loop would break on filenames with spaces. The cron line is missing a field.",
  "plan": "Rewrite backup.sh cleanly (correct default config, manifest written in one pipeline), fix the config and cron line, make the script executable, and run it.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > /app/ops/backup.sh <<'EOF'\n#!/bin/bash\n# Nightly backup of the application data directory.\nset -euo pipefail\n\nCONF=\"${BACKUP_CONF:-/app/ops/backup.conf}\"\nsource \"$CONF\"\n\nmkdir -p \"$DEST_DIR\"\ncd \"$SRC_DIR\"\ntar -czf \"$DEST_DIR/$ARCHIVE_NAME\" .\n\nfind . -type f -name \"$MANIFEST_GLOB\" -print0 | sort -z | xargs -0 -r sha256sum > \"$DEST_DIR/MANIFEST.txt\"\n\necho \"backup ok: $DEST_DIR/$ARCHIVE_NAME\"\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "chmod +x /app/ops/backup.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -i 's/^DEST_DIR = /DEST_DIR=/' /app/ops/backup.conf\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -i 's/^30 2 \\* \\* root/30 2 * * * root/' /app/ops/backup.cron\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "/app/ops/backup.sh; echo \"exit=$?\"\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

